LED toggle
The previous example was a nice introduction to LEDs and buttons. Now we are after something a bit more complex. We want the button to toggle the state of the LED every time we press it. How would you do this? What makes this more complex than the previous case? Try to figure out ways to implement this, even if it doesn’t fully work yet.
The code below shows a way forward. The key issue is that we need to detect an event - the button being pressed, rather than a state. The event corresponds to a change of state, so to detect the event, we keep track of the state and its changes. If the current state of the button pin is high, but was low before, then the button must have been pressed between the last two cycles of the main loop. So we change the state of the LED at this point.
Try the code, and see if it works. You may play with the delay at the end, uncommenting it and changing the value. Anything unexpected?

